       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's usual adult dose is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the maximum. 50 mg is five times that ceiling and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or worse in a 70 kg patient.\n\nThis may be a typo (5 mg, or possibly 10 mg), but I can't tell which was intended, and I shouldn't guess at a dose for a patient.\n\nAlso, medication orders normally need to come from a licensed prescriber. If you're not one, please pass this to the medicine team so the attending or a covering prescriber can enter or confirm it.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms the intended dose, send it to me and I'll enter it. If the intended dose is 50 mg, they should confirm that directly and document the reason before it goes in."
      }
